# Who has to look before something lands.
#
# keys/ is the one that matters. Everything this feed publishes is signed with its
# own key, and what decides whether an upstream's bytes are worth signing is
# whether their public key is in that directory. A pull request adding one is not
# a configuration change; it is the whole trust decision, made once, in a diff
# that is four lines long and easy to wave through.
#
# The rest are here because they decide what runs: tools/ executes against
# upstream-controlled values, .github/ is the pipeline itself, and owfeed.yml
# names the URL and the key the feed publishes under.
#
# This does not replace review — it makes review unskippable. Pair it with branch
# protection requiring review from code owners, or the file is documentation.

*                   @VizzleTF

